  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 240 PM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge will remain over the area Friday into the\nweekend before starting to flatten some later this week. Highs \nwill continue to warm into the middle 90s to near 100 degrees \nagain Friday and Saturday, and possible again on Sunday, especially\nacross the southern portions of the area. A slightly drier air \nmass will start to move into the area late week, so dew points \nmay be slightly lower, but heat index values around 100 degrees \nare expected through at least Saturday. A Heat Advisory is in \neffect for the entire area through 8 PM Saturday.\n\nAn upper level trough will move south into the Plains late this\nweekend then will move northeast into the Great Lakes region\nearly next week. The trough will flatten the ridge some and send\na front south into the area later Saturday into Sunday. Shower \nand storm chances (30-70%) will occur Saturday evening into \nSunday with the best chances across the northern portions of the\narea closer to the upper level trough. With the upper level \nsupport remaining more to the north, rainfall amounts will \nlikely decrease to the southeast and not all locations could be \nimpacted by rain--especailly further south.\n\nA cooler air mass will move into portions of the area late this\nweekend into early next week. Highs are expected to range from \naround 80 across the north portions of the area to around 90 \nacross southern Missouri early next week as the upper level \ntrough and cooler temps remain north of the area.",
